{"w":2400,"h":3406,"lines":[{"y":0.042181259800960547,"c":1,"x":0.86966962256396374,"t":"Reading","w":0.089949289957682366,"h":0.018280616173377395},{"y":0.091569767485694675,"x":0.061855672754045847,"w":0.18762886047363281,"h":0.01453488361674482,"c":1,"t":"Questions 14-18"},{"c":1,"h":0.018907298358552094,"t":"Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.","x":0.063917521604655386,"y":0.12936046495486631,"w":0.38969072977701824},{"h":0.01614797416324143,"t":"Write the correct letter in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.","x":0.061855673145440736,"y":0.1670581329517089,"w":0.61443298339843755,"c":1},{"y":0.20346447451759631,"w":0.56082473754882822,"c":1,"t":"14 In the first paragraph, the writer makes a point that","x":0.059793816653421032,"h":0.017465758309669455},{"t":"the director should plan the sound track at an early stage in filming.","y":0.23106283012051776,"h":0.017615971814445186,"x":0.15670105080267718,"c":1,"w":0.68041234334309897},{"c":1,"h":0.017469172049324744,"w":0.777319590250651,"y":0.24999999972066034,"t":"it would be wrong to overlook the contribution of sound to the artistry of films.","x":0.15670102964115898},{"t":"C","x":0.10927835073613359,"h":0.01453488361674482,"y":0.26889534874395316,"w":0.016494844754536941,"c":1},{"x":0.10927835071551503,"t":"D","y":0.28779069760538722,"c":1,"h":0.014534883616744931,"w":0.016494844754536941},{"x":0.15670102611418288,"c":1,"t":"the music industry can have a beneficial influence on sound in film.","h":0.017441861012089888,"y":0.26889534856053965,"w":0.67835052490234371},{"t":"it is important for those working on the sound in a film to have sole","y":0.28736051832958287,"x":0.1566232990827395,"h":0.018906838041295337,"c":1,"w":0.67024688720703118},{"x":0.15670103320085763,"y":0.30668604666461463,"h":0.015988371754420472,"t":"responsibility for it.","c":1,"w":0.18969071706136068},{"c":1,"t":"15 One reason that the writer refers to Humphrey Bogart is to exemplify","y":0.33430232530489101,"w":0.7402061971028645,"x":0.059793808537712607,"h":0.017441861012089777},{"t":"the importance of the actor and the character appearing to have similar","w":0.72384195963541687,"y":0.36285678962057966,"c":1,"x":0.15251214068778979,"h":0.01842613970610385},{"y":0.38197768232444718,"h":0.016567891020671244,"x":0.15663361413210622,"c":1,"t":"personalities.","w":0.13621730804443363},{"t":"B","x":0.10927835071551503,"y":0.40116279052354686,"c":1,"w":0.016494844754536941,"h":0.013081395479069058},{"t":"C","y":0.42005813937632941,"c":1,"h":0.013081395479068947,"x":0.10721649458659954,"w":0.018556701342264809},{"t":"D","c":1,"w":0.016494844754536955,"h":0.014534883616744709,"y":0.43749999990674393,"x":0.10927835069489648},{"h":0.018694560106404023,"c":1,"w":0.70738052368164062,"y":0.39928975985301896,"x":0.15250702733194602,"t":"the audience's wish that actors are visually appropriate for their roles."},{"y":0.4200581397013502,"w":0.66597935994466151,"c":1,"h":0.015988371754420583,"t":"the value of the actor having had similar feelings to the character.","x":0.15257733021959732},{"y":0.4356620027843241,"c":1,"x":0.15249938662057702,"h":0.020789855939111423,"w":0.70738220214843739,"t":"the audience's preference for dialogue to be as authentic as possible."},{"w":0.51752578735351562,"h":0.017615971814445186,"x":0.059793807237610207,"c":1,"y":0.46652965348350994,"t":"16 In the third paragraph, the writer suggests that"},{"w":0.80618555704752604,"c":1,"t":"audiences are likely to be critical of film dialogue that does not reflect their own","h":0.017615971814445075,"x":0.14639175745322783,"y":0.49559600718711594},{"x":0.15652428578013797,"y":0.51278438989657804,"w":0.12211692810058597,"c":1,"h":0.017247678809353517,"t":"experience."},{"w":0.018556701342264809,"x":0.10721649458659954,"y":0.5334302323995852,"h":0.013081395479068947,"c":1,"t":"B"},{"c":1,"t":"C","y":0.5508720928647014,"w":0.018556701342264809,"h":0.013081395479068947,"x":0.10721649458659954},{"h":0.01453488361674482,"y":0.56831395339511592,"t":"D","x":0.10721649458659954,"c":1,"w":0.018556701342264809},{"t":"film dialogue that appears to be dull may have a specific purpose.","w":0.66597935994466151,"c":1,"h":0.017441859892096456,"y":0.53197674429813779,"x":0.15463919027509188},{"y":0.55079271882016156,"w":0.74020619710286462,"h":0.017615971814445075,"c":1,"x":0.1546391693779382,"t":"filmmakers vary considerably in the skill with which they handle dialogue."},{"w":0.67010309855143224,"h":0.015988371754420583,"x":0.15463917226704088,"y":0.5697674420272042,"c":1,"t":"the most successful films are those with dialogue of a high quality."},{"x":0.05765455988494949,"w":0.60426737467447911,"t":"17 What does the writer suggest about Bringing Up Baby?","h":0.019751763245811627,"c":1,"y":0.59586797770144062},{"x":0.15045768936021831,"c":1,"t":"The plot suffers from the filmmaker's wish to focus on humorous dialogue.","y":0.62419812456417656,"h":0.019797450013533169,"w":0.75270889282226561},{"y":0.64533176755811983,"h":0.01614797416324143,"c":1,"w":0.76701029459635406,"t":"The dialogue helps to make it one of the best comedy films ever produced.","x":0.14432990414540739},{"h":0.01453488361674482,"c":1,"t":"C","w":0.018556701342264809,"y":0.66279069758116249,"x":0.10721649458659954},{"t":"There is a mismatch between the speed of the dialogue and the speed of","y":0.6626247422422884,"w":0.74444742838541667,"h":0.018446674223724591,"c":1,"x":0.15045519075607405},{"x":0.15219454241154617,"w":0.083523413340250652,"h":0.017117130147381809,"c":1,"y":0.68082955177300508,"t":"actions."},{"x":0.14020617759543824,"t":"The nature of the dialogue emphasises key elements of the film.","h":0.017615971814445075,"c":1,"y":0.70052847930777518,"w":0.66391754150390625},{"x":0.057652662157577764,"y":0.72715682267914483,"t":"18 The writer refers to the 'click' of a door to make the point that realistic sounds","w":0.82489339192708333,"h":0.019276002401193981,"c":1},{"h":0.019094553402571934,"t":"are often used to give the audience a false impression of events in the film.","x":0.15252156048334106,"y":0.75609741423244936,"w":0.76092524210611978,"c":1},{"t":"may be interpreted in different ways by different members of the audience.","w":0.75463918050130208,"h":0.015988371754420583,"x":0.15257731688570686,"y":0.77616279086373918,"c":1},{"t":"C","c":1,"h":0.013081395479068947,"x":0.10721649503068439,"y":0.79505813937632941,"w":0.016494844754536941},{"w":0.018556701342264822,"y":0.81249999994827204,"c":1,"t":"D","h":0.01453488361674482,"x":0.10515463891649647},{"y":0.79213153232245526,"h":0.0189149792727763,"t":"may be modified in order to manipulate the audience's response to the film.","c":1,"x":0.15463917372853245,"w":0.76288660685221354},{"x":0.15051547644434057,"c":1,"h":0.017615971814445075,"y":0.81238989989810706,"t":"tend to be more significant in films presenting realistic situations.","w":0.65773193359374993},{"c":1,"t":"leltsresources.org","w":0.29150955200195311,"y":0.95429983519544526,"x":0.35218917419595402,"h":0.022623461971406189},{"t":"93","c":1,"h":0.01453488361674482,"x":0.92164948452208439,"y":0.9505813952192439,"w":0.028865979512532558}]}